   image gate: marshall_field_jr_house_1919_prairie cdn_almanac_1913: verdict "differs", 3 difference(s) open: the north flank's two-storey bays with flat tops (balconies over them) across the rear ranges, and the rear range's canted north bay the sheet draws: T-3337 builds the canted bay (u -14.5 to -9.4 on the sheet, 1.2 m out) flat-topped under a moulded stone cornice and a stone balustrade, with four-light stone-mullioned groups in both storeys; the quoined flat-topped block at the middle range's corner is not built; the steep gables over the rear ranges: the plate draws three or more, stepped and finialled at their peaks; T-3337 carries both ranges' gables up in a stone coping with kneelers and a turned finial at each apex (the two ranges' apexes stand at about 13.8 and 15.2 m, stepping up toward the alley); the third, smaller gable the plate shows at the flank's far end and the small pinnacled dormers between the gables are not built; the rear ranges' north flank against both Gatlin plates: through this camera the plate's two-storey flank runs on past the garage's north-east corner (about 50-80 px further from the tower than the render's) and its cornice stands higher in the frame, as though its north face stood nearer the street-side camera than the 1911 sheet's trace puts the ranges (v -3.1 and -4.8 m); the camera is fitted on the front block alone, so whether the ranges or the fit are out is not settled here
   image gate: marshall_field_jr_house_1919_prairie gatlin_programme_1919: verdict "differs", 4 difference(s) open: the rear ranges' roofs: the plate draws a broad gable over the rear range, steep gables stepping down the flank, each carried up in a pale stone coping finialled at its peak, and a row of small gabled dormers with pinnacles between them; T-3337 carries both ranges' gables up in a stone coping along each rake with a kneeler at each foot and a 0.6 m turned finial at the apex (K01's rear_wings[].roof.coping, as T-3301's street dormer); the row of small pinnacled dormers between the gables is not built; the north flank's two-storey bays with flat tops and their stone mullioned windows: T-3337 builds the 1911 sheet's canted north bay on the rear range (u -14.5 to -9.4, 1.2 m out where the sheet reads about 1.4), two storeys to the range's wall top, flat-topped under a moulded stone cornice and a stone balustrade, with a four-light stone-mullioned transomed group on its face in each storey and a sash in each cheek, the range's gable standing back over it; the quoined block at the middle range's north-west corner and its mullioned stretch are not built; the rear range's canted north bay: the plate draws it dark (brick or ivy) between the range's pale corners and does not resolve its own corners; built in brick with its stone-mullioned groups (T-3337) and no quoins of its own; the rear ranges' north flank against both Gatlin plates: through this camera the plate's two-storey flank runs on past the garage's north-east corner (about 50-80 px further from the tower than the render's) and its cornice stands higher in the frame, as though its north face stood nearer the street-side camera than the 1911 sheet's trace puts the ranges (v -3.1 and -4.8 m); the camera is fitted on the front block alone, so whether the ranges or the fit are out is not settled here
